IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdcsa-types`
IMPORT `cdcsa-common`
IMPORT `cdcsa-maternity-adoption`

-- Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 — GOALS 5 AND 6: FATHERS AND SHARED
-- PARENTAL LEAVE (paternity: ss 12H-12JA; shared parental leave for an April
-- 2025 Scheme child: ss 12DA-12DD and the Second Schedule; for an earlier
-- child, by the mother's election: ss 12E-12G).
--
--   "How many weeks of paternity leave, and how much pay; how many units of
--    shared parental leave does each parent have; how much may the employer
--    claim back; and what may a self-employed or Government-paid parent get?"
--
-- A "week-equivalent" is a period of the weekly index or 6 days, whichever
-- is lower: one week of work days. Source: ../source/CDCSA2001.txt lines
-- 2422-3624.

§ `Goals 5-6 — fathers and shared parental leave`

§§ `Paternity leave eligibility (s 12I(1)-(2))`

-- s 12I(1): a natural father: "(a) the mother's confinement ... occurs, or the
-- estimated delivery date ... is, on or after 1 January 2017, or (in the case
-- of a stillborn child) on or after 1 November 2021; (b) the child ... (i) is a
-- citizen ... at ... birth, or (in the case of a stillborn child) would have
-- been ...; or (ii) ... becomes a citizen ... within the period of 12 months
-- ...; (c) the child's mother [is or becomes lawfully married to him at
-- conception, before birth, or within 12 months after birth]; (d) in the case
-- of a male employee, he has served the employer for a period of at least 3
-- months preceding the date of the child's birth; and (e) [self-employed:
-- 3 months continuous]".
@ref s 12I(1)
GIVEN b IS A Birth, married IS A BOOLEAN, months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a natural father eligible for paternity leave, birth` b `, married in time:` married `, months of service` months IF
        `the confinement date gate` b
    AND (b's `a citizen at birth (or would have been, if stillborn)` OR `becomes a citizen within 12 months of birth` b)
    AND married
    AND months AT LEAST 3

-- s 12I(2): an adoptive father: "(a) the eligibility date ... is on or after
-- 1 January 2017; (b) the child is below 12 months of age on the eligibility
-- date ...; (ba)-(c) [citizenship where the child is a permanent resident or
-- foreign]; (d) ... served his employer for ... at least 3 months before the
-- eligibility date ...; (e) [self-employed: 3 months]; and (f) he is not the
-- natural father of the child".
@ref s 12I(2)
GIVEN a IS AN Adoption, months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an adoptive father eligible for paternity leave, adoption` a `, months of service` months IF
        `the eligibility date of` a AT LEAST YMD 2017 1 1
    AND months AT LEAST 3
    AND `the adoption conditions` a

§§ `Paternity leave and pay (ss 12H, 12I(3)-(4), 12J)`

-- s 12H(1): paternity leave "(a) ... within 16 weeks commencing on the date
-- of the child's birth: (i) in the case of the father of an April 2025 Scheme
-- child — a period of 4 weeks; (ii) in the case of the father of any other
-- child — a period of 2 weeks; or (b) one or more ... periods [totalling 4
-- times the weekly index or 24 days, or twice the weekly index or 12 days],
-- ... within 12 months".
-- s 12I(3): pay up to "(a) $2,500 for every period equal in duration to the
-- male employee's weekly index or every 6 days, whichever is the lower ...;
-- and (b) a total of — (i) $10,000 for the male employee who is the father of
-- an April 2025 Scheme child; or (ii) $5,000 ... any other child".
-- s 12J(1)-(2): the employer claims back the pay and its CPF contribution,
-- within the same limits.
@ref ss 12H(1)-(2), 12I(3), 12J(1)-(2)
GIVEN april IS A BOOLEAN, `gross per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Leave payments`
`paternity leave payments, an April 2025 Scheme child:` april `, gross pay per week` `gross per week` MEANS
    `Leave payments` WITH
        `weeks of paid leave`                        IS `weeks`
        `employer pays at most`                      IS `capped`
        `Government reimburses the employer at most` IS `capped`
    WHERE
        `weeks`  MEANS IF april THEN 4 ELSE 2
        `capped` MEANS `at most` 2500 `per block and` (`weeks` TIMES 2500) `in all, for` `weeks` `blocks paid at` `gross per week`

-- s 12H(1)(b)(ii): the flexible days: "(A) ... April 2025 Scheme child — 4
-- times the employee's weekly index or 24 days, whichever is the lower; or (B)
-- ... any other child — twice the employee's weekly index or 12 days".
@ref s 12H(1)(b)(ii)
GIVEN april IS A BOOLEAN, wi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the flexible paternity days, an April 2025 Scheme child:` april `, weekly index` wi MEANS
    IF april THEN `the lower of` 4 `times the weekly index` wi `or` 24
    ELSE `the lower of` 2 `times the weekly index` wi `or` 12

-- s 12H(4) and 12I(4): a self-employed father: "(i) in the case of the father
-- of a January 2024 Scheme child — 4 times his weekly index or 24 days ...;
-- or (ii) ... any other child — twice his weekly index or 12 days"; paid up to
-- $2,500 a week-equivalent and "a total of — (i) $10,000 for the self-employed
-- man who is the father of a January 2024 Scheme child; or (ii) $5,000". The
-- Act says January 2024 here and April 2025 for employees (NOTES, fork F4).
@ref ss 12H(4), 12I(4)
GIVEN jan2024 IS A BOOLEAN, `lost income per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government pays a self-employed father at most, a January 2024 Scheme child:` jan2024 `, lost income per week` `lost income per week` MEANS
    `at most` 2500 `per block and` (`weeks` TIMES 2500) `in all, for` `weeks` `blocks paid at` `lost income per week`
    WHERE
        `weeks` MEANS IF jan2024 THEN 4 ELSE 2

§§ `Government-paid paternity benefit (s 12HA, 12I(4A))`

-- s 12I(4A): "(a) ... the mother's confinement ... or the estimated delivery
-- date ... on or after 1 January 2021; or (ii) the eligibility date ... on or
-- after 1 January 2021, and the child is below 12 months of age ...; (b) for at
-- least 90 days in total during the period of 12 months immediately before
-- ... [employed or self-employed]; (c) [natural father: s 12I(1)(b), (c)];
-- (d) [adoptive father: s 12I(2)(c), (f)]; (e) [the overseas conditions]".
@ref s 12I(4A)-(4B)
GIVEN e IS A `Child event`, married IS A BOOLEAN, w IS A `Work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible for the Government-paid paternity benefit, event` e `, married in time:` married `, work` w IF
        w's `days employed or self-employed in the 12 months before` AT LEAST 90
    AND w's `the 90-day overseas conditions are met, if any days were outside Singapore`
    AND CONSIDER e
        WHEN `a birth` b THEN
                (b's `confinement on` AT LEAST YMD 2021 1 1 OR b's `estimated delivery date` AT LEAST YMD 2021 1 1)
            AND (b's `a citizen at birth (or would have been, if stillborn)` OR `becomes a citizen within 12 months of birth` b)
            AND married
        WHEN `an adoption` a THEN
                `the eligibility date of` a AT LEAST YMD 2021 1 1
            AND `the adoption conditions` a

-- s 12HA(2)-(3): "(a) an amount equivalent to 14 days of his total income; or
-- (b) in the case of an eligible father of a January 2024 Scheme child, ... 28
-- days", "an amount that does not exceed $2,500 for every 7 days". s 12HA(10):
-- (b) does not apply to a stillborn child (who is not a Scheme child anyway).
@ref s 12HA(2)-(3), (10)
GIVEN jan2024 IS A BOOLEAN, `income per day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government-paid paternity benefit at most, a January 2024 Scheme child:` jan2024 `, total income per day` `income per day` MEANS
    `at most` 2500 `per block and` (`blocks` TIMES 2500) `in all, for` `blocks` `blocks paid at` (7 TIMES `income per day`)
    WHERE
        `blocks` MEANS IF jan2024 THEN 4 ELSE 2

§§ `Extra paternity leave reimbursed (s 12JA)`

-- s 12JA(1): applies to a natural father where "(i) the confinement occurs
-- before 1 January 2024 but the estimated delivery date is on or after that
-- date; (ii) the confinement occurs on a date between 1 January 2024 and
-- 31 March 2025 (both dates inclusive), and the estimated delivery date is
-- before 1 April 2025"; or an adoptive father with an eligibility date between
-- 1 January 2024 and 31 March 2025.
@ref s 12JA(1)
GIVEN e IS A `Child event`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12JA applies to the child` e IF
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `a birth` b THEN
            NOT b's `stillborn`
        AND (   (b's `confinement on` LESS THAN YMD 2024 1 1 AND b's `estimated delivery date` AT LEAST YMD 2024 1 1)
             OR (    b's `confinement on` AT LEAST YMD 2024 1 1
                 AND b's `confinement on` AT MOST YMD 2025 3 31
                 AND b's `estimated delivery date` LESS THAN YMD 2025 4 1))
    WHEN `an adoption` a THEN
            `the eligibility date of` a AT LEAST YMD 2024 1 1
        AND `the eligibility date of` a AT MOST YMD 2025 3 31

-- s 12JA(2)(d): for each day of extra paternity leave the employer pays "(i)
-- if the employee's gross rate of pay is $2,500 or less for every period equal
-- in duration to the employee's weekly index or every 6 days (whichever is the
-- lower) (called the number of reimbursable days per week), ... his gross rate
-- of pay ...; (ii) if ... exceeds $2,500 ..., (A) his gross rate of pay ...; or
-- (B) an amount ... at least ... P/W where P is $2,500 and W is the number of
-- reimbursable days per week" (the formula is printed as an image).
@ref s 12JA(2)(d)
GIVEN `gross per week` IS A NUMBER, wi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the least an employer may pay per day of extra paternity leave, gross pay per week` `gross per week` `, weekly index` wi MEANS
    IF `gross per week` AT MOST 2500 THEN `gross per week` DIVIDED BY `W`
    ELSE 2500 DIVIDED BY `W`
    WHERE
        `W` MEANS `the lower of` 1 `times the weekly index` wi `or` 6

-- s 12JA(4): reimbursement up to "(a) $2,500 for every period equal in
-- duration to the male employee's weekly index or every 6 days ... of the
-- extra paternity leave ...; and (b) a total of $5,000"; 12JA(2)(c): at most
-- 2 weeks.
@ref s 12JA(2)(c), (3)-(4)
GIVEN `weeks taken` IS A NUMBER, `paid per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government reimburses extra paternity leave at most, weeks taken` `weeks taken` `, paid per week` `paid per week` MEANS
    `at most` 2500 `per block and` 5000 `in all, for` (IF `weeks taken` GREATER THAN 2 THEN 2 ELSE `weeks taken`) `blocks paid at` `paid per week`

§§ `Shared parental leave for an April 2025 Scheme child (ss 12DA-12DD; Second Schedule)`

-- Second Schedule para 5: "the maximum number of units, M, is — (a) 6, in
-- relation to an April 2025 Scheme child — (i) who is born before 1 April
-- 2025, but the estimated delivery date ... is on or after that date but
-- before 1 April 2026; (ii) who is born between 1 April 2025 and 31 March 2026
-- (both dates inclusive), and the estimated delivery date ... is before
-- 1 April 2026; or (iii) in respect of whom the eligibility date of the
-- application to adopt the child is between 1 April 2025 and 31 March 2026
-- ...; or (b) 10, in relation to any other April 2025 Scheme child."
@ref Second Schedule para 5
GIVEN e IS A `Child event`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`M, the maximum number of units for` e MEANS
    IF NOT `an April 2025 Scheme child` e THEN REFUSE "not an April 2025 Scheme child: ss 12DA-12DD do not apply"
    ELSE IF `six` THEN 6 ELSE 10
    WHERE
        `six` MEANS
            CONSIDER e
            WHEN `a birth` b THEN
                    (    b's `confinement on` LESS THAN YMD 2025 4 1
                     AND b's `estimated delivery date` AT LEAST YMD 2025 4 1
                     AND b's `estimated delivery date` LESS THAN YMD 2026 4 1)
                OR  (    b's `confinement on` AT LEAST YMD 2025 4 1
                     AND b's `confinement on` AT MOST YMD 2026 3 31
                     AND b's `estimated delivery date` LESS THAN YMD 2026 4 1)
            WHEN `an adoption` a THEN
                    `the eligibility date of` a AT LEAST YMD 2025 4 1
                AND `the eligibility date of` a AT MOST YMD 2026 3 31

-- s 12DD(1)(b): each parent's units "calculated in accordance with the
-- formula M/2 [an image in the PDF] unless that allocation is varied"; Second
-- Schedule para 6: 3 and 3, or 5 and 5. s 12DD(4), para 7: a sole parent has M.
@ref s 12DD(1)(b), (3)-(4); Second Schedule paras 6-7
GIVEN e IS A `Child event`, both IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the default units for a parent of` e `, both parents eligible:` both MEANS
    IF both THEN `M, the maximum number of units for` e DIVIDED BY 2
    ELSE `M, the maximum number of units for` e

-- s 12DD(1)(a), (d) and para 8(2), (3), (5): units are whole numbers, and
-- the two parents' units "must not in the aggregate exceed" M.
@ref s 12DD(1)(a), (d), (4)(a), (d); Second Schedule para 8(2)-(6)
GIVEN n1 IS A NUMBER, n2 IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a valid allocation of` n1 `and` n2 `units within M =` m IF
        `whole` n1 AND `whole` n2
    AND n1 AT LEAST 0 AND n2 AT LEAST 0
    AND n1 PLUS n2 AT MOST m
    WHERE
        `whole` x MEANS FLOOR x EQUALS x

-- Second Schedule para 8(4): "The balance of any partially consumed period of
-- entitlement that has a fractional value cannot be reallocated"; para 12(3),
-- 13(3): a fractional balance is forfeited. (Para 8's illustration: 5 units,
-- 3.5 consumed — one unit may be reallocated, 0.5 cannot.)
@ref Second Schedule paras 8(4), 12(3), 13(3)
GIVEN allocated IS A NUMBER, consumed IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the units that may be reallocated, allocated` allocated `, consumed` consumed MEANS
    IF allocated GREATER THAN consumed THEN FLOOR (allocated MINUS consumed) ELSE 0

-- Second Schedule paras 1(1), 14-16: an employee need not obtain the
-- employer's agreement to a variation notified within "a period of 4 weeks
-- commencing on" the child's birth (or the adoption eligibility date) — the
-- specified variation period — unless a Director, as para 16(2) allows
-- ("may ... require"), has required it after a s 16 defaulting event; after that period the employer's agreement is
-- needed (para 15). Paras 9-10: variations only before the end of 12 months
-- from the child's birth.
@ref Second Schedule paras 1(1), 9, 10, 14-16
GIVEN notified IS A DATE, start IS A DATE, born IS A DATE, `section 16 event` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`a variation notified on` notified `, specified variation period from` start `, child born` born `, a Director has required the employer's agreement under para 16:` `section 16 event` MEANS
    BRANCH IF notified AT LEAST `add years` born 1                   THEN "not permitted: after the 12 months from the child's birth"
           IF notified LESS THAN start PLUS 28 AND NOT `section 16 event` THEN "permitted without the employer's agreement"
           OTHERWISE                                                 "permitted only with the employer's agreement"

-- s 12DA(2)(a): shared parental leave "(i) one period equal in duration to N
-- whole weeks, ... within 26 weeks ... of the child's birth; (ii) one or more
-- ... periods ... equal to N times the employee's weekly index or N times 6
-- days, whichever is the lower, ... within 12 months".
-- s 12DB(1), (4)-(5): pay, and the employer's claim back, up to "(a) $2,500
-- for every period equal in duration to the employee's weekly index or every
-- 6 days (whichever is the lower) ...; and (b) a total of N times $2,500".
@ref ss 12DA(2), 12DB(1), (4)-(5)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `gross per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Leave payments`
`shared parental leave payments for` n `units, gross pay per week` `gross per week` MEANS
    `Leave payments` WITH
        `weeks of paid leave`                        IS n
        `employer pays at most`                      IS `capped`
        `Government reimburses the employer at most` IS `capped`
    WHERE
        `capped` MEANS `at most` 2500 `per block and` (n TIMES 2500) `in all, for` n `blocks paid at` `gross per week`

-- s 12DA(6), 12DB(2): a self-employed parent, N week-equivalents of lost
-- income, the same limits.
@ref ss 12DA(6), 12DB(2)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `lost income per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government pays a self-employed parent at most for` n `units, lost income per week` `lost income per week` MEANS
    `at most` 2500 `per block and` (n TIMES 2500) `in all, for` n `blocks paid at` `lost income per week`

-- s 12DC(2), (4)(a): shared parental benefits: "an amount equivalent to a
-- number of days of the eligible parent's total income, where ... the number
-- of days is calculated in accordance with the formula N × 7", up to "$2,500"
-- for every 7 days. s 12DC(5): not if entitled under s 12DA(2) or (6), or "the
-- claim is submitted by the parent after the date of the child's death".
@ref s 12DC(2), (4)(a), (5)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `income per day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the shared parental benefit at most for` n `units, total income per day` `income per day` MEANS
    `at most` 2500 `per block and` (n TIMES 2500) `in all, for` n `blocks paid at` (7 TIMES `income per day`)

§§ `Shared parental leave by the mother's election (ss 12E-12G)`

-- s 12F(1)(a): for a natural father, "(i) in the case of a child born alive —
-- (A) the confinement occurs before 1 July 2017 but the estimated delivery
-- date is on or after that date; or (B) the confinement occurs on a date
-- between 1 July 2017 and 31 March 2025 (both dates inclusive) and the
-- estimated delivery date is before 1 April 2025; (ii) in the case of a
-- stillborn child — (A) the confinement occurs before 1 November 2021 but the
-- estimated delivery date is on or after that date; or (B) the confinement
-- occurs on a date between 1 November 2021 and 31 March 2025"; (b) citizen at
-- birth or within 12 months; (c) married in time. No period of service.
@ref s 12F(1)
GIVEN b IS A Birth, married IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a natural father may take elected shared parental leave, birth` b `, married in time:` married IF
        `the dates fall within s 12F(1)(a)`
    AND (b's `a citizen at birth (or would have been, if stillborn)` OR `becomes a citizen within 12 months of birth` b)
    AND married
    WHERE
        `the dates fall within s 12F(1)(a)` MEANS
            IF b's `stillborn`
            THEN    (b's `confinement on` LESS THAN YMD 2021 11 1 AND b's `estimated delivery date` AT LEAST YMD 2021 11 1)
                 OR (b's `confinement on` AT LEAST YMD 2021 11 1 AND b's `confinement on` AT MOST YMD 2025 3 31)
            ELSE    (b's `confinement on` LESS THAN YMD 2017 7 1 AND b's `estimated delivery date` AT LEAST YMD 2017 7 1)
                 OR (    b's `confinement on` AT LEAST YMD 2017 7 1
                     AND b's `confinement on` AT MOST YMD 2025 3 31
                     AND b's `estimated delivery date` LESS THAN YMD 2025 4 1)

-- s 12F(1A): an adoptive father: a joint application with the adoptive
-- mother; "the eligibility date ... between 1 July 2017 and 31 March 2025 (both
-- dates inclusive)"; married in time; the citizenship conditions.
@ref s 12F(1A)
GIVEN a IS AN Adoption, married IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an adoptive father may take elected shared parental leave, adoption` a `, married in time:` married IF
        a's `joint application with spouse`
    AND `the eligibility date of` a AT LEAST YMD 2017 7 1
    AND `the eligibility date of` a AT MOST YMD 2025 3 31
    AND married
    AND ((NOT `a citizenship condition applies` a) OR a's `an applicant (or the joint applicant spouse) is a citizen on the relevant date`)

-- s 12E(8): "N" is "(a) the integer 1, 2, 3 or 4, as specified by the
-- appropriate applicant ... in her election"; (b) after her death, the whole
-- weeks of her unconsumed entitlement, at most 4.
@ref s 12E(5), (8)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a valid s 12E election of weeks` n IF
    n EQUALS 1 OR n EQUALS 2 OR n EQUALS 3 OR n EQUALS 4

-- s 12E(7)-(7A): the mother's entitlement "is reduced by N weeks, taken from
-- the last N weeks of that entitlement".
@ref s 12E(7)-(7A)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, weeks IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the mother's weeks after electing` n `weeks, from` weeks MEANS weeks MINUS n

-- s 12F(2)-(3), 12G(2): "$2,500 for every period equal in duration to the
-- male employee's weekly index or every 6 days ... and ... a total of N times
-- $2,500"; the employer claims back the same (s 12G(1)).
@ref ss 12E(2)-(3), 12F(2)-(3), 12G(1)-(2)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `gross per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Leave payments`
`elected shared parental leave payments for` n `weeks, gross pay per week` `gross per week` MEANS
    IF NOT `a valid s 12E election of weeks` n
    THEN REFUSE "s 12E(8): N must be 1, 2, 3 or 4"
    ELSE `shared parental leave payments for` n `units, gross pay per week` `gross per week`

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 12DA(3)-(14), 12DB(6)-(10), 12DC(6)-(10), 12DD(2), 12E(4), (5A), (9)-(15), 12H(1A), (3), (5)-(13), 12HA(4)-(9), 12J(3)-(5), 12JA(5)-(6); Second Schedule paras 2-4, 11-13, 17-18
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`fathers' and shared provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "ss 12DA(3), 12H(1A): notice of the prescribed period before taking leave as one block"
         "ss 12DA(4)-(5), 12H(3): termination forfeits unconsumed leave, unless shared parental leave units are reallocated under Second Schedule para 12"
         "s 12DA(7)-(9): an adoptive parent's leave starts on or after the eligibility date; entitlement ends the day after the child's death; once per confinement"
         "ss 12DB(6)-(9), 12DD(2): discretionary reimbursement where a parent lacks 3 months' service and an equivalent arrangement was voluntarily granted"
         "s 12DC(6)-(7): unpaid leave of 12 months, or loss by contract end or redundancy, does not disqualify"
         "s 12E(4), (5A), (7B)-(9B): the adoptive father's leave follows the eligibility date; the election's timing and irrevocability; the father's entitlement after the mother's death; forfeiture after 12 months or on leaving"
         "s 12H(5)-(6): an adoptive father's leave starts on or after the application or pass date; no dismissal notice during the leave"
         "s 12HA(4)-(6): the Government-paid paternity benefit is not paid to a father entitled to paternity leave, subject to unpaid leave and contract-end exceptions"
         "ss 12J(3)-(5), 12JA(6): discretionary reimbursement where the father lacks 3 months' service"
         "Second Schedule paras 2-4, 11-13, 17-18: one arrangement per confinement or adoption; variation after marriage or adoption; reallocation instead of forfeiture or on death; written notice, refusal and effect"
